-- title:
--   Fricke-twisted Weil pairing on J_H(M)[n]: nine properties
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \ge 1$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ and $n \ge 1$, and write $\bar F =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(M)$, with $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}, \bar F)$; assume every nonzero element of $\bar F$ has a degree-zero divisor recording its orders at all places. Let $e$ be a divisorial Weil-pairing datum for $(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}, \bar F, n)$, i.e. a map `e.pair` on the $n$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ with values in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ agreeing with the explicit evaluation pairing of every Weil datum and satisfying a moving lemma, and let $w$ be a $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $\bar F$, acting on $J_H(M)$ through `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut`, subject to three hypotheses: (hw1) for every prime $\ell$ and every choice of integrality, fundamental-identity, finiteness and norm-formula data for the two maps $\alpha,\beta$ from $\bar F$ to the level-$M\ell$ field, the transposed Hecke correspondence `heckePic0HBarTranspose` applied to $w \cdot x$ equals $w$ applied to `heckePic0HBar` of $x$; (hw2) $\langle d\rangle(w\cdot\langle d\rangle x) = w\cdot x$ for all $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, where $\langle d \rangle$ is `diamondHBar`; (hw4) if $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ acts on $M$-th roots of unity by $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^c$ with $c$ coprime to $M$, then $w\cdot(\sigma \cdot x) = \sigma\cdot\langle c\rangle(w \cdot x)$. Let finally $B : J_H(M) \times J_H(M) \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ be any function with $B(x,y) =$ `e.pair` $x\,(w\cdot y)$ whenever $nx = ny = 0$. The conclusion is the conjunction of nine statements about $n$-torsion arguments: $B(x,y)^n = 1$; additivity in the first and in the second variable (multiplicatively in the values); left non-degeneracy ($B(x,-) \equiv 1$ forces $x = 0$); the equivariance $B(\langle c\rangle(\sigma x), \sigma y) = \sigma(B(x,y))$ for $\sigma$ and $c$ as in (hw4); self-adjointness of `heckeOperatorHAlong` at every prime $\ell$ and of every $\langle d\rangle$; right non-degeneracy; and that every subgroup $A \le J_H(M)$ killed by $n$ equals its double annihilator, i.e. an $n$-torsion $x$ pairing trivially with every $n$-torsion annihilator of $A$ lies in $A$.
--
--   This packages the Fricke- (Atkin–Lehner-) twisted Weil pairing on the $n$-torsion of the Jacobian of $X_H(M)$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, for which Hecke and diamond operators become self-adjoint and Galois acts through the twist by $\langle c\rangle$, with the pairing datum and the twisting automorphism named rather than merely asserted to exist. It is used in the analysis of the Néron model of $J_H$ at $p$, where annihilator counts for toric and cyclotomic parts of component groups are compared via this pairing.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_pairing_nsmul_eq_zero_galois_heckeH_diamondH_biannihilator_of_divisorialWeilPairingData_frickeAlgEquiv.lean

import Mathlib
